{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512936-improving-the-success-chance-of-grail-embrace-~da-v20","id":1512936,"title":"Improving the success chance of Grail Embrace [~DA V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-27T02:31:02-07:00","id":1512936,"title":"Improving the success chance of Grail Embrace [~DA V20]","content":"The Grail Embrace is a powerful ritual described in the Ashen Knight book.<br /> <br /> The system is quite simple:<br /> 1) The player rolls Conscience + Courage +Road rating (Chivalry, Heaven or Humanity) at a Difficult of 6<br /> 2) The Storyteller rolls 10 + Generation Background at Difficult of 6<br /> 3) Both keep rolling until the end of the ritual.<br /> The first who accumulates 10 successes wins. If both rolls 13 times without accumulating 10 successes the Grail Embrace fails and the ritual could be repeated in the following years. If the Storyteller wins the ritual fails and can not be repeated (and probably the Vampire may suffer significant damage). If the player wins the Embrace is successful.<br /> <br /> We usually play with a reasonable mix of rules from multiple editions. When possible we use the most recent rules or the ones we feel are the most balanced. We use DA V20 as a base with a lot of material from previous editions.<br /> How do I increase success chance while maximizing character generation? Obviously one should maximise Conscience Curage and the Road rating. And probably maximising also Willpower to gain automatic success on the roll. The roll is quite unique so one needs generic bonuses such as reroll, additional dice or reduced difficulties. So far I have thought of the lucky merit to avoid catastrophic failure and luck (DA V20 companion) incantation to make a charm that reduces the difficulty of a roll by 2.<br /> <br /> Any other good ideas?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T03:19:57-07:00","id":1512937,"title":"","content":"I don't think you should imrpove the ritual, it suposed to be hard and dangerous; the Cainite basically throwing titself at the mercy of God! If God sees the supplicant sincere, the curse is lessened in a HUGE way (or if not, while not destroyed, quite painfull)<br /> Your Beast is &quot;conquered&quot;<br /> You don't need to feed<br /> Sunlight and fire is only lethal<br /> No more R\u00f6tchrek<br /> The snow-like palor of your skin glows like a halo<br /> You can't drink Cainite vitae and Blood Oaths are broken<br /> Your blood creates &quot;super ghouls&quot;<br /> Protection from True Faith<br /> I mean Jesus Christ (excuse the pun)! <br /> <br /> To be honest I would even make it <i>harder </i>to achieve this state<br /> BUT if you really want to improve the success chance, I suggest - depending of the Character's deeds eg. how <i>worthy </i>the Cainite is in God's eyes (chance to role play it out, wove sotries about a young cursed knight achieved this) simply lower the difficulity of the player's rolls and raise the difficulity of the Beast's/Storyteller's rolls to reflect this (or opposite, if you want to make it harder)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T03:46:45-07:00","id":1512938,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that sounds like something functionally indistinguishable from Golconda. Or close enough.<br /> <br /> In that light, bare minimum the PC attempting to receive the benefits of this ritual should have to go on a personal journey that spans most of a chronicle. Having to prove their resolve, purity of intentions, and capacity for nobility. We're talking &quot;Knight of the Round Table looking for the Holy Grail&quot; levels of personal character arc. Which, given the name, sounds like the intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T13:04:24-07:00","id":1512997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512936-improving-the-success-chance-of-grail-embrace-~da-v20?p=1512937#post1512937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you should imrpove the ritual, it suposed to be hard and dangerous; the Cainite basically throwing titself at the mercy of God! If God sees the supplicant sincere, the curse is lessened in a HUGE way (or if not, while not destroyed, quite painfull)<br /> Your Beast is &quot;conquered&quot;<br /> You don't need to feed<br /> Sunlight and fire is only lethal<br /> No more R\u00f6tchrek<br /> The snow-like palor of your skin glows like a halo<br /> You can't drink Cainite vitae and Blood Oaths are broken<br /> Your blood creates &quot;super ghouls&quot;<br /> Protection from True Faith<br /> I mean Jesus Christ (excuse the pun)!<br /> <br /> To be honest I would even make it <i>harder </i>to achieve this state<br /> BUT if you really want to improve the success chance, I suggest - depending of the Character's deeds eg. how <i>worthy </i>the Cainite is in God's eyes (chance to role play it out, wove sotries about a young cursed knight achieved this) simply lower the difficulity of the player's rolls and raise the difficulity of the Beast's/Storyteller's rolls to reflect this (or opposite, if you want to make it harder)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I also agree that if anything it should be HARDER and not easier in any way. The benefits are huge, it's like a &quot;final test&quot; of faith for a character in this kind of arc. In my games, even though I don't make it harder per se, in the sense of making the rolls harder or anything, I make failure mean death. Failing the ritual utterly destroys the Cainite as it's burnt by the Grail's blood inside him. I also highlight the fact that the Ashen Knight's scholars themselves are not quite sure about the nature of the blood, because as we already discussed in another topic, the ritual fails in humans, so what it is truly, in the end, remains a <b>mystery</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T23:40:30-07:00","id":1513044,"title":"","content":"These seams to be quite generic comments, from a storyteller's POV, that could be made for any ambitious or interesting player's objective.<br /> <br /> I do not think that making the roll harder adds anything from the game perspective, If the players do not have any control over the roll then it is only a gamble and the whole point in making it the &quot;final test&quot; of faith becomes dumb.<br /> If you are proposing to rework the whole mechanics to create a longer path to achieve the mechanical reward of the Grail Embrace with multiple quests along the way and where the action of the player has a clear impact on the final test, then I may be interested. If you are suggesting that the beast dice pool should be increased by 7 dice and that is it I think that your suggestion is uninspiring and anticlimatic.<br /> <br /> From the vampire's POV, it makes sense to search for all possible ways to succeed in the Embrace, the most obvious way is to embrace humanity (or one of the other roads) and its virtues. Then he/she may look for other ways to prepare for its last fight with the Beasts. For example, the incantation rule could be used to provide a mechanical effect to an important token of faith obtained at the end of a pilgrimage to a sanctuary devoted to penitence and atonement. Or it may be an invocation to the saint patron of redeemed sinners or of penitents.<br /> <br /> The idea that we should rely on God's mercy is not the only idea of salvation in Christianity, different theories of salvation arose during history and some of them require the active contribution of the faithful.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think that the Grail Embrace is an interesting opportunity from a game perspective:<br /> 1) Drinking blood became a choice and not a need, this strongly increases the ethical tension in the use and consumption of blood.<br /> 2) You can probably be a &quot;functional&quot; vampire even during the day (high road rating plus only lethal damage from sunlight), but this clearly increases the risk of being discovered and identified as a vampire, again a new tension between returning to a semblance of life and following your mission as an ashen knight<br /> 3) You are clearly a supernatural being, this may rise suspicious and attract undesired attention.<br /> 4) If the groups would like to explore PVP dynamics, the huge change in the character may alter its relationship with the remaining vampires.<br /> <br /> I think that the Grail Embrace could be more interesting if it has more downsides, maybe random, that strengthen the ethical tension due to being at the same time a vampire and a good guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T13:39:52-07:00","id":1513107,"title":"","content":"You could take the Merits &quot;Self-Confident&quot; and &quot;Charmed Existence&quot; from the second edition players guide (both 5 pts).<br /> <br /> With &quot;Self-Confident&quot; if you spend a Willpower Point to buy an automatic success on a roll, you get the point back if you roll at least one success on the roll.<br /> <br /> &quot;Charmed Existence&quot; lets you simply ignore a single rolled 1 on every roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> You could get the first do in the &quot;Path of Mars&quot; which allows you to increase you courage for one scene by 1 point.<br /> <br /> The 5ht dot of &quot;Path of the Focused Mind&quot; would allow you reduce the difficulsty of every action for one scene by -2, but I'm not sure id those checks are actions.<br /> <br /> There is also the level 5 Ritual Lion Heart (I think from the second edition The Players Guide to the Sabbat) courage +3 for 20 minutes, but but that has the dis advantage that you need to rest within 2h after the end of the Ritual, or you start to lose health levels at a rate on 1 level per 10 minutes.<br /> But you could use the level 5 ritaul &quot;Vires acquirit eundo&quot; (Bloodmagic revised edition) or the level 6 &quot;Ritual of Holding&quot; (second edition players guide) to extend it's duration.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 05-28-2023, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T19:14:56-07:00","id":1513149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512936-improving-the-success-chance-of-grail-embrace-~da-v20?p=1513107#post1513107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Charmed Existence&quot; lets you simply ignore a single rolled 1 on every roll.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably the most useful merit in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T21:14:25-07:00","id":1513262,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your kind suggestions.<br /> <br /> I already thought of the 5th dot of &quot;Path of the focused mind&quot;, I was not sure that it could be useful in these specific circumstances but if it could be applied to the Grail Embrace rolls it would be a nice fit from a narrative point of view. The path was probably unknown to the Tremere of that time and the character should search for this knowledge by looking at older blood sorcery sources.<br /> <br /> War cray form path of Mars is definitely a good idea.<br /> <br /> The 5th level ritual is troublesome because the Grail Embrace lasts the whole night.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}